 {"id":"fabro-a08a","title":"Develop planner prompt: visit-1 fresh-cycle line to skip dead context reads","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T15:14:55.468Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T15:24:21.706Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 1, add one line: 'visit 1 with no current_seed_id in ## Context = fresh cycle; go straight to sd ready'. In run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8 the planner opened with two context_read calls at pass start, one erroring with unknown context key 'current_seed_id' because it was visit 1 and nothing existed to read (events seq 31-34). Expected effect: two fewer tool rounds per fresh planner pass (~$0.02, ~8 s of the 59.7 s stage); orthogonal to fabro-c3b4 (top-N view, output volume) and fabro-e4fa (call economy). Basis: run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8, workflow version af036506627c2c235dc58d52e1ceda475fc4053f219b513e9582f644224dc129, commit 6f23b48525bf1ff7b11d3a4c49ad43681a9ff1fb","labels":["revision","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-fc1b","title":"Implementer prompt: require the full touched-crate test suite when the seed touches tests","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T16:34:54.153Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:11:08.818Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 4, replace the 'ONE focused test' verification rule with: when the seed adds or edits tests in a crate, the pre-gate check is cargo nextest -p <touched-crate> (full crate suite), still never the workspace suite. Evidence from run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP: implementer@1 ran targeted fabro-server tests only and missed the two pre-existing Docker-socket failures (run_start_grants_github_token_bridge_only_to_user_principals, worker_principal_run_without_vault_token_takes_no_token_path) that live in the full fabro-server suite; the resulting gate-red bounce (tester@1 340s + implementer@2 915s/$0.769 + tester@2 91s) cost ~22 min, ~40% of the 55-min run wall, to apply a 6-line [run.environment] id = \"local\" pin. Expected effect: pre-existing or adjacent breaks in the touched crate surface in the same implementer pass, eliminating ~20 min / ~$0.8 per bounce of this class. Distinct from closed seeds fabro-0d56/fabro-2254 (fmt/clippy scope) which cover lint checks, not the test-suite scope. Basis: run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP, workflow version 8aedc5a9bbdd71b2f882af0b6c7d28a947212553646a31a390f5d173a91c8a69, commit 9966d125e665593fcd4f21137a19659625d58ed0","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-8d1c","title":"ADR-0019: record the engine-provided-credentials doctrine in the ADR file itself (PR #68 landed prompts-only)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:11:58.469Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:37.132Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"ADR-0019 doctrine extension (PR #68: 'treat engine-provided credentials as agent-reachable capabilities') landed ONLY in workflow prompts (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md step 5, .fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md capability paragraph) - the ADR file itself (docs/lab/adr/0019-capability-gate-for-agent-surfaces.md) does not mention engine-provided credentials at all: no reference to the GITHUB_TOKEN injection via resolve_workflow_env (lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/services.rs), the git credential bridge (lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/git_bridge.rs), or the rule that a diff merely USING an engine-provided credential on a new code path is a capability delta requiring recorded user approval.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: the ADR is the durable decision record; prompts get rewritten by every revision pass and are agent-reachable surface themselves. Reviewers, revisors, and future grill sessions cite ADR-0019 - if the record omits the engine-provided-credential class, the gate doctrine silently narrows back to container-env-visible capability on the next prompt rewrite (exactly the PR #53 blind spot the extension closed).\n\nFIX: add one paragraph to ADR-0019 Decision section (or a numbered extension like .7) stating: engine-provided credentials and bridges (GITHUB_TOKEN injection, git credential bridge) ARE agent-reachable capability; diffs that use them on new code paths are capability deltas requiring recorded user approval; cite PR #68, run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8, and the fabro-16ff user directive (2026-09-08). Docs-only change, no code.\n\nBasis: agent sweep of other-machine runs 2026-09-08 evening, commit e078c27b2 (PR #68) vs docs/lab/adr/0019-capability-gate-for-agent-surfaces.md, commit 47b491b8e (repo state).","labels":["revision"]}
-{"id":"fabro-85a1","title":"merge-upstream: full-history clone (run.clone depth=0) - shallow clone broke range math in 3 consecutive merge runs","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:37.228Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:37.228Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"The shallow-clone trap hit THREE consecutive merge-upstream runs (01M20E43YS, 01M20N60ZY, both merge+reviewer nodes journaled it with 'Do not keep rediscovering this'): the run sandbox clone arrives at depth 100 (.git/shallow boundary e.g. 43036bb477), so git rev-list --count origin/denkhaus..upstream/main reports a misleading ~4919 and git merge-base returns nothing until the merger unshallows mid-pass (~8s). Commit a4850e681 fixed this for the CONDUCTOR survey only ([run.clone] depth = 0 in .fabro/workflows/conductor/workflow.toml) - the merge children are their own workflow and .fabro/workflows/merge-upstream/workflow.toml has NO [run.clone] section, so every merge child still rediscovers the trap. Each child run clones origin/denkhaus fresh at creation (conductor workflow.toml comment).\n\nFIX: add [run.clone] depth = 0 to .fabro/workflows/merge-upstream/workflow.toml, mirroring the conductor commit a4850e681 (volume is ~neutral - the survey's unbounded git fetch upstream already pulls the full shared history into the shallow clone each pass, ~150 MB either way, measured). Alternative considered and rejected: a merger-procedure is-shallow guard + git fetch --unshallow is per-pass remediation, not a fix.\n\nBasis: journals .fabro/journal/01M20E43YS004DCEYPJ0GJQH4B.jsonl and 01M20N60ZY6DZDTX60WW0161KP.jsonl (merge v1 + reviewer v1 painpoints), agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["engine"]}
+{"id":"fabro-85a1","title":"merge-upstream: full-history clone (run.clone depth=0) - shallow clone broke range math in 3 consecutive merge runs","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:37.228Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:32:38.736Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"The shallow-clone trap hit THREE consecutive merge-upstream runs (01M20E43YS, 01M20N60ZY, both merge+reviewer nodes journaled it with 'Do not keep rediscovering this'): the run sandbox clone arrives at depth 100 (.git/shallow boundary e.g. 43036bb477), so git rev-list --count origin/denkhaus..upstream/main reports a misleading ~4919 and git merge-base returns nothing until the merger unshallows mid-pass (~8s). Commit a4850e681 fixed this for the CONDUCTOR survey only ([run.clone] depth = 0 in .fabro/workflows/conductor/workflow.toml) - the merge children are their own workflow and .fabro/workflows/merge-upstream/workflow.toml has NO [run.clone] section, so every merge child still rediscovers the trap. Each child run clones origin/denkhaus fresh at creation (conductor workflow.toml comment).\n\nFIX: add [run.clone] depth = 0 to .fabro/workflows/merge-upstream/workflow.toml, mirroring the conductor commit a4850e681 (volume is ~neutral - the survey's unbounded git fetch upstream already pulls the full shared history into the shallow clone each pass, ~150 MB either way, measured). Alternative considered and rejected: a merger-procedure is-shallow guard + git fetch --unshallow is per-pass remediation, not a fix.\n\nBasis: journals .fabro/journal/01M20E43YS004DCEYPJ0GJQH4B.jsonl and 01M20N60ZY6DZDTX60WW0161KP.jsonl (merge v1 + reviewer v1 painpoints), agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["engine"]}
 {"id":"fabro-ad74","title":"merge-upstream touchpoints.md: refresh two stale paths (web header.tsx moved, improve.md retired)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:50.477Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:50.477Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"The merge-upstream reviewer burned a grep pass producing false MISSING on two stale paths in .agents/skills/merge-upstream/references/touchpoints.md (run 01M20N60ZY6DZDTX60WW0161KP, reviewer v1 painpoint): (1) 'web header.tsx' actually lives at apps/fabro-web/app/routes/run-detail/header.tsx (src->app layout move), (2) scripts/prompts/improve.md no longer exists (retired per ADR-0015, prompt embedded in the revisor workflow - documented in scripts/run_workflow.nu header). The reviewer noted: 'Platform asset - next maintainer should refresh the touchpoints table paths; I did not modify it.'\n\nFIX: refresh the two rows in touchpoints.md to the current paths; while there, add a one-line maintenance note that the table is verified against the tree by the reviewer probe each pass, so path drift is caught at the next pass instead of causing false MISSING.\n\nBasis: journal .fabro/journal/01M20N60ZY6DZDTX60WW0161KP.jsonl reviewer v1 painpoint, agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-5ff7","title":"Revisor: harden the duplicate check - sd show every analyst-cited seed id, sd list is capped at 50","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:50.572Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:19:50.572Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"TWO revisor passes nearly mis-dropped or mis-kept findings because the tracker picture was capped: (a) run 01M20RX5E6P91DRT64CRCMAHGQ analyze v1: sd list --format compact returned exactly 50 rows and hid open seeds (fabro-a0e3, fabro-c3b4, fabro-9ef9, fabro-4811, fabro-270c) that per-theme sd search then surfaced - 'a list-only duplicate check would have mis-dropped or mis-kept findings'. (b) run 01M20XGWE2ZYM9ADRM2PVE322F analyze v1: sd list capped at 50 AND sd search returned empty for themes matching analyst-cited seeds by title+description (e.g. 'qualitygate transient deterministic' vs fabro-4815) - 'the revisor step should mandate sd show on every seed id cited in the analyst answer, or sd list with an explicit raised limit'. fabro-c16d covers the PLANNER-side default --limit 50; this seed covers the REVISOR-side duplicate check.\n\nFIX: in .fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md (tracker command reference + analyze step): mandate sd show <id> for EVERY seed id cited in the analyst answer before judging duplicate/drop (statuses and titles verified individually), and treat sd list as a summary view only; where the analyst cites themes without ids, require sd search per theme AND a raised-limit sd list --limit 200 fallback. Evidence: in pass (b) sd show verification was done ad hoc and caught everything - make it mandatory.\n\nBasis: journals .fabro/journal/01M20RX5E6P91DRT64CRCMAHGQ.jsonl and 01M20XGWE2ZYM9ADRM2PVE322F.jsonl analyze v1 painpoints, agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-8c1e","title":"Revisor + closeout prompts: document sd priority number->band mapping (1=High, 2=Medium, default 2)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.207Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:20:09.207Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"sd's --priority is a 0-4 number (P0-P4) where 1=High, 2=Medium, 3=Low, default 2 - NOT intuitive at filing time. Run 01M20RX5E6P91DRT64CRCMAHGQ file v1 painpoint: 'sd create output reports Medium priority though both findings requested priority 2 - verify sd's priority number->band mapping in the CLI help before filing if exact High/Medium matters' (fabro-e4c4 and fabro-a08a landed Medium though the revisor's intent read as High-band work). IN-SESSION REPRODUCTION (agent sweep, 2026-09-08 evening): the agent filed fabro-8d1c with --priority 2 intending High and had to correct it to 1 afterwards - same trap, second consumer.\n\nFIX: one documentation line in .fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md tracker command reference (sd create row): 'priority bands: 0=P0 1=High 2=Medium 3=Low 4=Lowest; default 2 - pass 1 explicitly for High findings'. Optionally the same line in the develop closeout prompt where seeds get filed. Docs-only.\n\nBasis: journal .fabro/journal/01M20RX5E6P91DRT64CRCMAHGQ.jsonl file v1 painpoint + agent reproduction (fabro-8d1c priority correction), agent sweep 2026-09-08 evening, commit ccf927888.","labels":["revision"]}
